menu "E1-Mic module"

    config E1_SELFTEST_DAC
        bool "Enable DAC loopback self-test"
        default n
        help
            Drives the ESP32 cosine-wave generator on a DAC pin so the board can
            feed its own ADC a known tone, with no external instrument. Requires
            a jumper wire from the DAC pin to the ADC input (GPIO34).

            Leave this OFF for the real module: GPIO25 is not connected to
            anything in the Kundt schematic.

    config E1_SELFTEST_DAC_GPIO25
        bool "Use GPIO25 (DAC channel 0)"
        depends on E1_SELFTEST_DAC
        default y
        help
            GPIO25 is DAC channel 0, GPIO26 is channel 1. Unset to use GPIO26.

    config E1_SELFTEST_DAC_FREQ
        int "Self-test tone frequency (Hz)"
        depends on E1_SELFTEST_DAC
        range 130 20000
        default 1200
        help
            1200 Hz matches the AD9833 default of module E2. The RTC-driven
            cosine generator cannot go below about 130 Hz.

endmenu
